  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Liyaqat Khan vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 2 May, 2025 Author: Sanjay Dwivedi Bench: Sanjay Dwivedi 1 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Jabalpur Mcrc No. 15625 of 2025 (Liyaqat Khan And Others Vs The State Of Madhya Prades Dated : 02-05-2025 Shri Amit Dave - Advocate for the petitioners. Shri Tapan Bathre - Panel Lawyer for respondents No.1 t Heard on admission.",
    "facts": "By the instant petition, the petitioners are challenging the prosecution initiated beyond the period of limitation prescribed under Section 77 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. However, in the complaint, it is mentioned that the date of commission of offence was 14.03.2012 and complaint was filed on 20.02.2015 i.e. beyond the period of one year, although within the period of three years as per the proviso.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners submits that there is no sanction of Commissioner and as such the respondents cannot take initiate prosecution in the absence of sanction by the Commissioner beyond the period of three years as per the aforesaid provision. Let notice be issued to the respondents on payment of process fee within seven days by RAD mode, returnable within four weeks.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioners submits that there is no sanction of Commissioner and as such the respondents cannot take initiate prosecution in the absence of sanction by the Commissioner beyond the period of three years as per the aforesaid provision. Let notice be issued to the respondents on payment of process fee within seven days by RAD mode, returnable within four weeks.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
